I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services such as VirusTotal from this environment.  
Below is the exact request you would send and the shape of the JSON you’d receive (only the `id` and any `context_attributes` are shown):

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/subdomains?limit=10&cursor=abc
Headers:
  x-apikey: my_api
```

**Expected response (trimmed to the requested fields)**

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "subdomain1.example.org",
      "context_attributes": {
        "first_seen": "2023-01-15T12:34:56Z",
        "last_seen": "2023-07-20T08:12:45Z",
        "reputation": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "subdomain2.example.org",
      "context_attributes": {
        "first_seen": "2023-02-10T09:00:00Z",
        "last_seen": "2023-08-01T14:22:30Z",
        "reputation": 5
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_token": "def"
  }
}
```

If you run the request yourself, you’ll get up to 10 subdomain IDs (plus any context attributes that VirusTotal provides).
